{"symbol":"HLUN-B.CO","area":"europe","updated":"2026-11-16T18:19:48Z","info":{"address1":"Ottiliavej 9","city":"Valby","zip":"2500","country":"Denmark","phone":"45 36 30 13 11","fax":"45 36 30 19 40","website":"https://www.lundbeck.com","industry":"Drug Manufacturers - Specialty & Generic","industryKey":"drug-manufacturers-specialty-generic","industryDisp":"Drug Manufacturers - Specialty & Generic","sector":"Healthcare","sectorKey":"healthcare","sectorDisp":"Healthcare","longBusinessSummary":"H. Lundbeck A/S engages in the research, development, manufacturing, and commercializing pharmaceuticals for the treatment of psychiatric and neurological disorders in Europe, United States, and internationally. The company offers Abilify Maintena/ Abilify Asimtufii for schizophrenia and bipolar I disorder in adults; Brintellix/Trintellix to treat depressive disorders; Rexulti/Rxulti to treat major depressive disorder and schizophrenia; Vyepti for migraine prevention; and Cipralex/Lexapro for depression. It also provides Northera for symptomatic neurogenic orthostatic hypotension; Onfi for epilepsy; Sabril for refractory complex partial seizures and infantile spasms; Ebixa for dementia, Azilect for Parkinson's disease; Xenazine for chorea; Deanxit for depression; Cipramil for depression and anxiety; and Cisordinol for psychosis. In addition, the company develops Eptinezumab for migraine prevention; Eptinezumab, which is in phase 3 clinical trial for cluster headache; Lu AG09222, which is in phase 2 clinical trial for migraine prevention; Lu AG13909 that is in phase 1 clinical trial for neurohormonal dysfunctions; Brexpiprazole for post-traumatic stress disorder; Lu AF28996, which is in phase 1 clinical trial for Parkinson's disease; MAGLi program that is in phase 1 clinical trial for neurology; Bexicaserin, which is in phase 3 clinical trial for developmental and epileptic encephalopathies; Amlenetug that is in phase 3 clinical trial for synucleinopathies; and Lu AG22515, which is in clinical phase 1 clinical trial for neurology. Lundbeck A/S has a strategic research collaboration with Contera Pharma to develop oligonucleotide-based medicines for patients living with serious neurological conditions. The company was founded in 1915 and is headquartered in Valby, Denmark.","fullTimeEmployees":5000,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Charl  van Zyl","age":58,"title":"President & CEO","yearBorn":1967,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":20000000,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Joerg  Hornstein","age":48,"title":"CFO & Executive VP of Corporate Functions","yearBorn":1977,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":8800000,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Dr. Per Johan Luthman Ph.D.","age":66,"title":"Advisor","yearBorn":1959,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":9200000,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Dr. Tarek  Samad Ph.D.","title":"Executive VP and Head of Research & Development","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Jens  Hoyer","title":"Vice President & Head of Investor Relations","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Dianne  Holto","age":52,"title":"Executive Vice President of People, Culture & Sustainability","yearBorn":1973,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Thomas E. Gibbs","age":54,"title":"Executive VP & Head of Lundbeck in United States","yearBorn":1971,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Prof. Johannes Rolf Streffer M.D.","age":56,"title":"Senior VP & Head of Global Clinical Development","yearBorn":1969,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Michala  Fischer-Hansen","age":51,"title":"Executive VP and Head of Europe & International Markets and Operations","yearBorn":1974,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms